From 19985a7ecd8f049aa698889829c00094a7a95f24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CafeDead <cafedead@CafeDeaddeMac-Mini.local>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:26:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(qwen3): declare a dense recompute policy for layer
 selection

selection.source=model_adapter_safe_regions requires ModelAdapterSpec.recompute;
only DeepSeek-V4.1 declared one, so Qwen3 dense could not use layer_count or
layer_indices. Every Qwen3 decoder layer is one safe region (no cross-layer
state producer/consumer, no non-decoder execution branch), so the policy is a
single region pattern with no exclusions or runtime hook.

With a policy installed, mode=full without an explicit selection auto-upgrades
to the adapter regions, so existing full-recompute baselines change behavior
and must be re-measured.
---
 .../policies/activation_checkpointing.py      | 32 +++++++++++++
 .../models/qwen3/adapter/registration.py      | 10 ++++
 .../models/qwen3/test_recompute_policy.py     | 48 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 90 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hyper_parallel/models/qwen3/adapter/policies/activation_checkpointing.py
